// @run
// @log 1.5
// @log 63
// @log 1
// THE OTHER HALF of `load-width-in-named-fn-with-lambda.vl`, and the control that
// makes its failure mean something: in a module with NO function value anywhere,
// a named function wrapping a load width compiles and runs. One variable changes
// between the two cases — whether the module uses a lambda — so the failure over
// there is attributable to capture analysis and to nothing about the widths.
//
// 0x3FC00000 (f32 1.5) at address 0 is the bytes 00 00 C0 3F, so the byte at
// offset 3 is 0x3F = 63 — the top byte of the float, read through the same
// memory the f32 load reads.
function peekF32(a: i32): f32 { __load_f32__(a) }
function peekByte(a: i32): i32 { __load_u8__(a) }
function pages(): i32 { __memory_size__() }

__store_i32__(0, 0x3FC00000)
print(peekF32(0))
print(peekByte(3))
print(pages())
